From 43aa8aeaeeffbdd50bc7998bc43029bcf32fac4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:48:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: what the zoom to the active area does, or
 why not

With "Zoom to the active area of Dolby Vision videos" on, the video page
of the player information has a row, under what leaves the device, that
says what the zoom does now (the area and how many times larger the
picture is drawn) or why it does nothing: no active area in the video's
Dolby Vision data, data that do not fit the picture, no black bars, a
screen that already shows the picture as large as it can, another view
mode, a disc menu, 3D. In plain words, in the four languages of Hades.

The renderer keeps what it drew where it already tells kodi.log
(ACTIVEAREA::Shown, set only when that changes), and the window system
reads it when it publishes the player information: nothing is computed
on the way of a picture. The reasons are named constants, the same
texts as in the log, told apart by their text (WhyOf()).

system/hades made again (make-playerinfo.py).
---
